From 596fef44b9f90bd08bf2dd7124b1cdb03dfb818a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:40:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [AGS] sys_events.cpp: fix three more gaps in patch 0017's
 own file

Extends patch 0017's own incomplete coverage, not a fresh unrelated
finding -- same file 0017 already ported, three more real gaps only a
continued full build (not the earlier scratch-stub isolation check)
could surface, since sys_events.cpp's own body has functions later in
the file that isolation check didn't need to reach.

- SDLK_a/SDLK_z -> SDLK_A/SDLK_Z (6 call sites): SDL3 renamed these
  constants to uppercase (SDLK_A's own value is still the lowercase-'a'
  keycode, 0x61 -- purely a name capitalization change, not a semantic
  one, confirmed by reading SDL_keycode.h directly). SDL3 ships
  SDL_oldnames.h as an opt-in compatibility layer (SDL_ENABLE_OLD_NAMES),
  but its *default*, unguarded branch deliberately redefines old names
  like `SDLK_a` to a broken `SDLK_a_renamed_SDLK_A` sentinel so
  un-migrated code fails loudly at compile time instead of silently
  miscompiling -- this is intentional SDL3 tooling, not a gap in SDL3
  itself, and defining SDL_ENABLE_OLD_NAMES to paper over it would be
  the wrong direction for a real port. Did the real rename instead,
  matching this whole patch series' own practice. Breadth-checked: built
  the full list of ~580 SDL_oldnames.h "renamed" macros and grepped
  Engine/+Common/ against all of them -- every other hit is either a
  comment, a non-DOS platform file that never compiles here (macOS/
  Android/iOS/Windows/OpenGL), or a coincidental substring match on an
  unrelated identifier -- SDLK_a/SDLK_z were the only two real old-name
  uses anywhere in the reachable tree.

- Utf8::GetChar(..., &ki.UChar) at line 311: a new instance of the
  established DJGPP int32_t-vs-int divergence category (patches 0013/
  0018/0019's category), here via a Utf8::Rune* (Utf8::Rune is int32_t)
  function parameter. KeyInput::UChar (Common/ac/keycode.h) is a plain
  int, used as a plain int everywhere else it's read (game_run.cpp,
  dialog.cpp, cscidialog.cpp, guitextbox.cpp) -- changing its own type
  would ripple needlessly, so fixed at the call site instead, matching
  0013/0019's own established precedent: reinterpret_cast<Utf8::Rune*>
  (&ki.UChar). Breadth-checked: every other Utf8::GetChar call site in
  the tree already uses a properly-typed Utf8::Rune local (string_utils.cpp
  x3, string_types.h) -- this was the only site passing a raw int*.

- std::truncf()/std::roundf() (3 call sites, calc_relative_delta() and
  set_t2m_pos()): AGS's own code calls these f-suffixed names directly
  in std::, a non-standard extension some libstdc++ configurations
  expose (_GLIBCXX_USE_C99_MATH_TR1) that DJGPP's does not -- patch
  0012's dos_compat.h already defines std::trunc(float)/std::round(float)
  (the suffixless, properly-overloaded C++ names) built on top of the
  same ::truncf/::roundf DJGPP builtins, so this is a one-line extension
  of that existing shim, not a new mechanism: re-expose them under the
  suffixed name AGS's call sites actually use. Breadth-checked: grepped
  Engine/+Common/ for every std::(round|trunc|ceil|floor|sqrt|sin|cos|
  tan|exp|log|pow|fabs|fmod|atan|asin|acos)f call and every std::(log2|
  exp2|fma|asinh|acosh|atanh)[fl] call -- these three sites (all in
  sys_events.cpp) are the only ones in the whole tree.

Verified: sys_events.cpp.obj compiles clean, zero errors. Full
cmake --build ... -- -k (keep-going) re-run: no new errors from this
file anywhere in the build.
---
 Common/platform/dos_compat.h | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp     | 14 +++++++-------
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Common/platform/dos_compat.h b/Common/platform/dos_compat.h
index 0ff07e02c..d87731ee2 100644
--- a/Common/platform/dos_compat.h
+++ b/Common/platform/dos_compat.h
@@ -120,6 +120,23 @@ namespace std {
     inline long double atanh(long double x) { return ::atanhl(x); }
 }
 
+// --- std::truncf / std::roundf: called directly by AGS's own code ---
+//
+// Engine/ac/sys_events.cpp calls std::truncf()/std::roundf() (the
+// f-suffixed name) directly, rather than relying on overload resolution
+// to pick the float overload of std::trunc()/std::round() -- this is a
+// non-standard extension some libstdc++ configurations expose
+// (_GLIBCXX_USE_C99_MATH_TR1) that DJGPP's does not. The plain
+// std::trunc(float)/std::round(float) overloads just above already do
+// this exact work; only the suffixed spelling itself is missing here.
+// Found by build-testing patches 0020-0023, confirmed narrow (grepped
+// every std::(round|trunc|...)f call in Engine/ and Common/: exactly
+// these two sites, both in sys_events.cpp).
+namespace std {
+    inline float truncf(float x) { return std::trunc(x); }
+    inline float roundf(float x) { return std::round(x); }
+}
+
 // --- std::mutex / std::condition_variable: absent under DJGPP ---
 //
 // DJGPP's libstdc++ is built without _GLIBCXX_HAS_GTHREADS (confirmed:
